# Every variable docker compose reads from .env in this deployment.
#
# You normally never create .env by hand: bootstrap.sh / the Deployment
# Wizard write it (mode 600, git-ignored) and toggle-features.sh keeps
# COMPOSE_PROFILES in step. This file documents what may appear there.
# Values here are examples; copy a line into .env only when you need it.
# See documentation/07-06-environment-variables.md.

# Keycloak's master-realm admin password. Keycloak reads it only on its
# first boot against an empty keycloak_data volume; changing it later has no
# effect (documentation/08-03-admin-password-and-break-glass.md). Written by
# bootstrap.sh. Unset, it falls back to the demo default "admin".
# KEYCLOAK_FIRST_BOOT_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional compose profiles that a plain `docker compose up -d` includes.
# local-eseal: the in-stack stamping service (documentation/10-local-e-sealing.md).
# Written by bootstrap.sh / toggle-features.sh. Never add "wizard" here: the
# wizard is started on demand with --profile wizard.
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=local-eseal

# Customized hosts only: the release compose file plus an overlay file
# (documentation/09-11-start-at-boot-backups-and-customized-hosts.md).
# COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:/path/to/overlay/compose.overlay.yml

# Deployment Wizard: the host address its port 8443 is published on.
# Default 127.0.0.1 (reach it through an SSH tunnel). 0.0.0.0 opens it on
# every interface - only on a trusted admin network, and remember Docker's
# published ports bypass host firewalls such as ufw.
# WIZARD_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1

# Deployment Wizard: extra names/IPv4 addresses for its self-signed
# certificate, when you browse to it by the host's address instead of
# through the tunnel. Comma-separated.
# WIZARD_TLS_SANS=10.0.0.42,padsign-host.internal
